{{Quote|The regional governors now have direct control over their territories.|Grand Moff Wilhuff Tarkin, governor of the Outer Rim Territories|<ref name="Episode 4">{{Film|IV}}</ref>}}
'''Governor''' was a [[Politics|political]] title used by high-ranking leaders of political territories, including [[planet]]s, [[moon]]s, and [[The galaxy|galactic]] regions.<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref>

==History==
[[File:GovernorWing.png|thumb|250px|left|Wing served as Governor of Calodan during the New Republic era.]]
In the late [[Republic Era]], [[Tok]] was a [[human]] who served as a governor for the [[Galactic Republic]].<ref name="Jango Fett 3">[[Jango Fett 3|''Jango Fett'' 3]]</ref> However, Tok actually served as an undercover [[agent]] for [[Count]] [[Dooku]], who planned to destabilize the Republic.<ref name="Jango Fett 4">[[Jango Fett 4|''Jango Fett'' 4]]</ref> In their governorship capacity, Tok worked to establish a peace<ref name="Jango Fett 3" /> between the [[Anselmi–Nautolan war|actively warring]]<ref name="Jango Fett 1">[[Jango Fett 1|''Jango Fett'' 1]]</ref> [[Nautolan]] and [[Anselmi]] peoples.<ref name="Jango Fett 3" /> In truth, however, Tok was tasked by Dooku with ensuring the war<ref name="Jango Fett 4" /> continued to rage<ref name="Jango Fett 1" /> so as to hurt the Republic.<ref name="Jango Fett 4" /> [[Sio Bibble]] was [[Governor of Naboo|governor]] of [[Naboo]] during the last days of the Republic.<ref name="Sio Bibble">{{Databank|sio-bibble|Sio Bibble}}</ref>

In the [[Galactic Empire]], governors held regional power under the Imperial regime<ref name="Episode 4" /> and assumed control over entire [[star system]]s, often in the name of stealing their resource wealth.<ref name="Who's Boss">{{InsiderCite|224|Who's the Boss?}}</ref> [[Sector]] governors were known as [[Moff]]s.<ref name="Tarkin" /> An Imperial governor could wear a standard [[Imperial military uniforms|Imperial uniform]], in the case of [[Arihnda Pryce]],<ref name="Steps">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Steps Into Shadow]]''</ref> or a [[Color|white]] [[Clothing|outfit]], as donned by [[Ubrik Adelhard]].<ref name="Uprising" /> Imperial governors also wore [[rank insignia plaque]]s consisting of six blue squares over three red and three yellow.<ref name="Uprising" /><ref name="Steps" /> [[Wilhuff Tarkin]] was governor of the [[Outer Rim Territories]]<ref name="Spark" /> under his rank of [[Grand Moff]].<ref name="Tarkin" /> Beyond the term governor referring to his actual power over the Rim,<ref name="Spark" /> he continued to be widely known as "Governor" as a honorific title.<ref name="Tarkin" /> By [[2 BBY]],<ref name="Date note">''[[Dawn of Rebellion]]'' dates the events of ''[[Star Wars Rebels: Steps Into Shadow]]'' seventeen [[Standard year|years]] after the end of the [[Clone Wars]], which ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates to [[19 BBY]]; therefore, the events of ''Steps Into Shadow'' must take place in [[2 BBY]]. According to ''[[Star Wars: On the Front Lines]]'', [[Mon Mothma]]'s denunciation of the [[Galactic Empire]] and the [[Declaration of the Rebel Alliance]] take place 2 years before the [[Battle of Yavin]] or [[2 BBY]]. As "[[Imperial Supercommandos]]" is set between ''Steps Into Shadow'' and "Secret Cargo," the events of the episode must also take place in 2 BBY.</ref> [[Gar Saxon]] was the [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Viceroy]] and Governor of [[Mandalore]]<ref name="Imperial Supercommandos">{{Rebels|Imperial Supercommandos}}</ref> of [[Clan Saxon|his clan]],<ref name="Zero Hour" /> a planet under [[Occupation of Mandalore|occupation]] of the Galactic Empire at the [[time]].<ref name="Out of Darkness">{{Rebels|Out of Darkness}}</ref>

